          <Pad Id="US0kRxRTDy7UdT1kEkSwLh" Bounds="290,391,420,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Switch Space and watch the origin and the size of one unit.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">7</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="pOTBqBKWQ4L4W41I1N8Bnd" Bounds="85,470,830,160" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Space is a property of the whole scene: the same elements, only the origin and the size of one unit change. y points down in all four spaces, as in Skia (CommonSpace of VL.Skia).&#xD;&#xA;- Normalized: origin at the center of the window, 1 unit = half the window height. The height runs from -1 (top) to 1 (bottom), the width from -W/H to W/H, and the unit follows when the window is resized.&#xD;&#xA;- DIP: origin at the center, 1 unit = 100 DIP. DIP are the device independent (logical) pixels of Qt.&#xD;&#xA;- DIPTopLeft: like DIP, origin at the top left corner. This is the default and what the other help patches use.&#xD;&#xA;- PixelTopLeft: origin at the top left, 1 unit = 100 device pixels (100 / dpr DIP). Independent of the DPI scale: at 150 % scaling 1 unit is 66.7 DIP, so the elements keep their size in physical pixels.&#xD;&#xA;- Without a window (QtTexture, QtRenderer [Stride]) the device pixel ratio is 1, so PixelTopLeft equals DIPTopLeft there. The scene size is the size of the texture or viewport.&#xD;&#xA;- Values that come back from the scene (Scene Bounds, pointer positions) are in units of the chosen space.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
